Scope. The MIT licence above covers the code and documentation written by
the authors. The outputs of that code in this package (results/, figures/,
weights/, weights_sens/, stb/run_outputs/ and the run outputs under tm/) and
the separate archive compute-aware-wsn-v1.5-cells.zip are released under
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), without prejudice to the terms
of the data they are derived from.

Third-party data are covered by neither licence, wherever they appear (in
inputs/ and inside stb/STB_frozen_2026-10-09.zip, including preprocessed
copies of them such as inputs/intel_*.npy). The Intel Berkeley Research Lab
data (inputs/intel_*.npy, inputs/intel_time_rows.csv, inputs/mote_locs.txt)
are from P. Bodik, W. Hong, C. Guestrin, S. Madden, M. Paskin and
R. Thibaux, "Intel Lab Data", 2004,
http://db.csail.mit.edu/labdata/labdata.html, whose page states: "Permission
is granted to use or reproduce this data in any format or venue, although we
request that you acknowledge our hard efforts in any published work.";
the Numenta Anomaly Benchmark files are distributed by Numenta, Inc.
under the MIT licence (Copyright 2014-2024 Numenta Inc.; LICENSE.txt of
github.com/numenta/NAB at commit ea702d75), whose notice is reproduced in
inputs/nab/LICENSE_NAB.txt. The SensorScope Grand St Bernard file
(inputs/sensorscope/stbernard-meteo.zip, unmodified) is by G. Barrenetxea,
"Sensorscope Data," Zenodo, 2019, doi:10.5281/zenodo.2654726, licensed under
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0). All are included
for reproducibility only and remain subject to their own terms.
